\begin{align*}
180 &= 168 \cdot 1 + 12 \\
168 &= 12 \cdot 14 + 0
\end{align*}
\] Since the remainder is 0, the GCF of 180 and 168 is the last non-zero remainder, which is 12. </think> <answer> 12 </answer>

